        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e7853267b2824671bd62fd1643ef8cab",
      "statement": "The loop guard maintains a sliding window of 5 stringified (tool name, sorted-args JSON, result JSON) triplets; when all 5 entries are identical the cycle aborts. Including the result in the key lets legitimate async polling (same call, evolving result, e.g. heygen_get_agent_session) survive while still catching a truly stuck loop.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L249-L256",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:147595389aa423f0e073dd3bfc302579d09caabe5cd189a1480ed15670cc89ff:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L389-L424",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cebdfbe1b5940684bc3fc5dd75f571f223893b6d66c0a97bb1052d4124f2f40a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_562a4a1b3dde459da10882b682e6c7cb",
      "statement": "When cycles are exhausted or a loop is detected, the engine appends a completion hint summarizing executed tools plus up to 3 quoted phrases from must rules, then makes a final generate call that still carries the tool schema; if that response has tool calls they are executed and a closing tool-less inference produces the final text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L426-L502",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe225cd40c7040d0a865b7df6ababf1baffc553fc33bd6ddf93ba92ba220e52a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e6b5b5fa8188488aad7993ae66456745",
      "statement": "_run_tool_calling_cycle() returns the full accumulated message history (cycle_messages) alongside the output and tool log, so must-compliance correction cycles chain from the complete tool context rather than a collapsed text summary.",
